* GnuCap simulation — gpio_analog_sensing
* Voltage divider: 3V3 -> R_fixed(10kΩ) -> V_mid -> R_sensor -> GND
*
* Three operating conditions swept:
*   node 2 — bright light photoresistor (~1kΩ)
*   node 3 — dim light photoresistor (~50kΩ)
*   node 5 — potentiometer at 5kΩ midpoint

V_3v3_A  1 0 DC 3.3
R_fixed_A 1 2 10000
R_bright  2 0 1000

V_3v3_B  10 0 DC 3.3
R_fixed_B 10 3 10000
R_dim     3 0 50000

V_3v3_C  20 0 DC 3.3
R_fixed_C 20 5 10000
R_pot     5 0 5000

* Sweep supply voltage to verify divider behaviour across full range
.dc V_3v3_A 0 3.3 0.1

* Print all three midpoint voltages
* GnuCap 2017 does not emit column headers in batch mode.
* Output column order: V_3v3_A | v(2) bright | v(3) dim | v(5) pot-mid
* At 3.3 V: v(2)~0.30 V (LDR 1kΩ), v(3)~2.75 V (LDR 50kΩ), v(5)~1.65 V
.print dc v(2) v(3) v(5)

.end
